  {
    "episode_id": 90864,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90864.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 13,
    "turn_text": "But I would say a little naive. I don't want to be I don't want to be mean to her. But yes, something like that. Listen, she was the Democrats expert on on banning plastic. She was their environmental. She's actually a professor who was teaching a class at a school I'll leave unnamed. And she was talking about the environmental quality and the injustice of the plastic industry. That was literally what her class was. And so why I'm sitting there watching her throughout the process and then I heard her five minute testimony. I looked at it and I thought that's very hypocritical. That you're saying that you're wanting to band all plastics And so the first question I asked her, which you know, you're never really supposed to ask a question unless you know the answer. But I just kind of I just threw my script out of the way and I said, ma'am, what are your glasses made out of? And she says, I don't know. And I said, what? You don't know? I said, it's made out of plastic. She says, I don't think they are. And I said, yes, they are. They're made out of plastics. And then I said, well, what's your phone made out of? And she says, it's not plastic. And I said, are you kidding me? Your phone isn't made out of plastic. There's no question about it. And then I talked to her about her cup. And she says, my cup's not plastic. This is a plastic. I said, ma'am, you're a lid. is plastic. And I just went through the process. I talked about her having petroleum products, which is plastic in your clothes. We all have those, if your clothes aren't stretchy, then maybe you don't, but most clothes like most people want their clothes a little stretchy right now, they have a petroleum based product in them. They have plastic in them. And everything, the vehicle you ride in is made out of plastic. And what my point was at the end of it, I said, ma'am, if this is what you believe, then don't use plastic. Live it. That means walk on wooden shoes and where I guess leather clothes, all leather clothes at first, which way to say the environmentalists don't want you to cut down trees and they don't want you killing animals either. So I don't know what you're wearing. I guess you're going to wear a plant base. And the last time I checked, plant-based clothing doesn't really hold up that well. And so it was just the point of just trying to expose the hypocrisy of these environmentalists that they don't think beyond today they think just based on emotion because they thought beyond today they'd realize that the very thing that they're protesting they are using and contributing to every single day.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
